GPEC DIII-D-like DCON Example
==============================

This example uses a synthetic DIII-D-like equilibrium generated by the tokamak equilibrium maker (tMaker). The equilibrium file ``TkMkr_D3Dlike_inexp=1.0.geqdsk`` is a 257x257 grid EFIT-format equilibrium with major radius ~1.68 m, toroidal field ~2.02 T, and plasma current ~1.2 MA, closely resembling a standard DIII-D H-mode configuration. Corresponding kinetic profiles (ion density, electron density, ion temperature, electron temperature, and toroidal angular frequency) are provided in ``TkMkr_D3Dlike_inexp=1.0.gpeckf``.

Unlike the DIII-D ideal and kinetic examples which run the full GPEC workflow, this example focuses exclusively on running DCON and illustrates the difference between an ideal MHD stability calculation and one augmented with the kinetic Euler-Lagrange equation.

Before running, ensure that ``equil.in`` has the correct path to the equilibrium file::

  eq_filename="TkMkr_D3Dlike_inexp=1.0.geqdsk"


Run 1: Ideal DCON (kin_flag=f)
--------------------------------

In this first run we compute ideal MHD stability using the standard Euler-Lagrange equation, with ``kin_flag=f`` in ``dcon.in``. The integration proceeds outward from near the magnetic axis to the plasma-vacuum interface defined by ``psiedge=0.988``, and the safety factor termination is handled explicitly via ``qhigh=20.2`` and ``sas_flag=f``. We also enable ``termbycross_flag=t`` so that the ODE solver terminates cleanly at zero crossings.

Make sure ``kin_flag = f`` in ``dcon.in``, then run::

>>  dcon

   DCON START => v1.5.5-323-g32985ece
   __________________________________________
   Forming the equilibirum
     Equilibrium: TkMkr_D3Dlike_inexp=1.0.geqdsk, Type: efit
     Jac_type = hamada, power_bp = 0, power_b = 0, power_r = 0
     psilow  = 1.000E-02
     psihigh = 9.900E-01
     etol =  1.000E-07
   Evaluating Mercier criterion
     q0 =  1.209E+00, qmin =  1.209E+00, qmax =  5.257E+00, q95 =  4.505E+00
     sas_flag = F, dmlim =  2.000E-01, qlim =  5.257E+00, psilim =  9.900E-01
     betat =  1.289E-02, betan =  1.344E+00, betap1 =  6.074E-01
     nn =    1, mlow =  -12, mhigh =   21, mpert =   34, mband =   33
   Fourier analysis of metric tensor components
   Computing F, G, and K Matrices
   Starting integration of ODE's
     psi = 1.000E-02, q =  1.211
     psi = 6.196E-01, q =  2.000
     psi = 8.113E-01, q =  3.000
     psi = 9.091E-01, q =  4.000
     psi = 9.832E-01, q =  5.000
     > Vacuum code overriding r 1.00E+00 from vac.in, to be 0
     psi = 9.900E-01, q =  5.257
   Re-Integrating to peak dW @ qlim =  5.222749, psilim =  0.989267
     psi = 1.000E-02, q =  1.211
     psi = 6.196E-01, q =  2.000
     psi = 8.113E-01, q =  3.000
     psi = 9.091E-01, q =  4.000
     psi = 9.832E-01, q =  5.000
     psi = 9.893E-01, q =  5.223
   Computing free boundary energies
   Energies: plasma = -9.238E-01, vacuum =  2.161E+00, real =  1.237E+00, imaginary =  4.359E-05
   All free-boundary modes stable for nn =  1.
   Total cpu time =  4 seconds
   Total wall time =  5 seconds
   PROGRAM STOP => Normal termination.


The positive real total energy (1.237E+00) confirms that the plasma is ideally stable to n=1 perturbations. The plasma energy is negative (-9.238E-01), meaning the plasma is drive-destabilising, but the stabilising vacuum contribution (2.161E+00) more than compensates. The ``Re-Integrating`` step reflects ``psiedge=0.988`` triggering a search for the peak dW location, which is found just inside the nominal boundary at psilim~0.989. The negligible imaginary component (4.359E-05) indicates no resistive instability.


Run 2: Kinetic DCON (kin_flag=t)
----------------------------------

In this second run we augment the ideal Euler-Lagrange equation with kinetic contributions from thermal ions and passing particles. DCON reads kinetic profiles via the PENTRC module using the ``kinetic_file`` specified in ``pentrc.in``, which has already been set to ``TkMkr_D3Dlike_inexp=1.0.gpeckf`` in this example. The file provides psi-dependent columns: ni (m\ :sup:`-3`), ne (m\ :sup:`-3`), Ti (eV), Te (eV), and omega_EXB (rad/s).

Set ``kin_flag = t`` in ``dcon.in`` and confirm the following flags are active as specified in the provided ``dcon.in``::

  kin_flag       = t    ! Activates kinetic Euler-Lagrange equation
  con_flag       = t    ! Continue integration through singular layers
  ion_flag       = t    ! Include ion kinetic energy contribution
  electron_flag  = f    ! Electron contribution excluded
  passing_flag   = t    ! Include passing particle effects
  trapped_flag   = t    ! Include trapped particle effects
  kinfac1        = 1.0  ! No scaling on energy contribution
  kinfac2        = 1.0  ! No scaling on torque contribution
  kingridtype    = 0    ! Regular radial grid for kinetic matrix

The kinetic profiles are read from ``TkMkr_D3Dlike_inexp=1.0.gpeckf``, which provides psi-dependent ni, ne, Ti, Te, and toroidal rotation frequency omega_E on a uniform psi grid. These profiles are used internally by the kinetic integration subroutine.

Run::

>>  dcon

   Using 4 threads

   DCON START => v1.5.5-323-g32985ece
   __________________________________________
   Forming the equilibirum
     Equilibrium: TkMkr_D3Dlike_inexp=1.0.geqdsk, Type: efit
